**Convention 1.3 (mathematical provenance).** The contribution here is
the composition of complete fractional-contact groups, their coordinate
faces and their one-dimensional contrast images into an exact criterion
for minimum original counts on a supplied attained face. This is a
repo-derived conditional deduction in ordinary mathematical prose; no
Lean/kernel verification is claimed. RC Theorem 69.1 already supplies the
eight signed tests, their nonidentity and the 24 endpoint-contact bound;
RC Theorem 70.1 and GC Theorem 15.1 supply compatibility and merge loss.
GC Proposition 12.2 supplies the common-law dictionary and compact
attainment, GC Proposition 10.1 the common constructor, and GC.10 the
minimum-total-count dictionary. None is a new result here. The
eight-low face extrema, nine-low existence bound and necessary nine-low
ranks are also credited to GC §§16–17 and FA Theorem 90.1.

Finite-polytope faces, connected edge graphs and Farkas alternatives are
ordinary finite convex geometry, used inside the composition rather
than claimed as new theorems. For the continuous moment interface,
di Dio–Schmüdgen, *The multidimensional truncated Moment Problem:
Atoms, Determinacy, and Core Variety*,
[arXiv:1703.01497v2, Lemma 3 and Proposition 4](https://arxiv.org/html/1703.01497v2),
supplies the zero-integral support principle and the
Richter–Tchakaloff dimension bound. They do not identify original
fractional labels with endpoint nodes. Dette–Melas, *A note on the
de la Garza phenomenon for locally optimal designs*,
[arXiv:1105.3575v1, §3 Theorem 1](https://arxiv.org/html/1105.3575v1),
requires its Chebyshev systems and distinguished information-entry
hypotheses. The eight-component moment table below has three zero
coordinates on its entire pure sheet; an eight-function Chebyshev
determinant on that sheet cannot be assumed. No Loewner-improvement
map preserving original contrast, capacity and absolute height is
supplied. Neither literature interface gives an eight- or seven-low
compression theorem here. No worldwide priority claim is made.

